==English==

===Etymology===
Origin unknown.
Possibly derived from "tosheroon" (5 crowns) therefore something of minimal worth.


Nonsense. "The slang tosh is a blend of the words 'trash' and 'bosh.' Bosh comes from the Turkish word for empty. Tosh means 'nonsense' or 'empty, worthless talk.'" (contributed by Sebastian Chen)

"...and don't give me any more of this listening to the news tosh!" 
- Vernon Dursley to Harry (OP1)

